4.2.6 Addendum to the Article:
In case the PSP is utilized as the ESS component, it may be located at a different location as a standalone component. In this case, all charges (including transmission charges and losses) associated with the charging of such ESS component shall be borne by the RPD.
9.4 In case SECI/Buying Entity(ies) decides to buy such discrete component’s power outside the PPA, such power shall be purchased at 50% of the Applicable Tariff. … In case SECI/Buying Entity(ies) decides to buy such discrete component’s power outside the PPA, Buying Entity shall specify the Peak Hours on daily basis, and such power shall be purchased at the following tariffs:
(i) for power supplied during Peak Hours (as specified by the Buying Entity), @ PPA Tariff;
(ii) for power supplied during non-solar hours, other than Peak Hours, @75% of the PPA Tariff;
(iii) for power supplied during solar hours, other than Peak Hours, @50% of the PPA Tariff. … Amendments in PSA document
1.3 … In case the Buying Entity decides to buy such discrete component(s) power outside the PPA/PSA, such power shall be purchased at 50% of the Applicable Tariff as per Article 1.1 above, for the applicable Contract Year. … In case the Buying Entity decides to buy such discrete component(s) power outside the PPA/PSA, Buying Entity shall specify the Peak Hours on daily basis, and such power shall be purchased at the following tariffs:
(i) for power supplied during Peak Hours (as specified by the Buying Entity), @the Applicable Tariff as per Article 1.1 above, for the applicable Contract Year;
(ii) for power supplied during non-solar hours, other than Peak Hours, @75% of the Applicable Tariff as per Article 1.1 above, for the applicable Contract Year;
(iii) for power supplied during solar hours, other than Peak Hours, @50% of the Applicable Tariff as per Article 1.1 above, for the applicable Contract Year.
